{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1792707305,"nonce":"JY/PXCJa2VY5kb3XLGVA5TYmmhA=","message":"Implementation and scoped validation\n\nThe active motion-subtree pool now uses cached_text::TextBatch. Preparation materializes collected polygon/path payloads with text_clip::prepare_glyphs, converts glyphs within that owning batch and appends with auxiliary rebasing. Dispatch uses the owned text renderer, which restores its rows and glyph atlases before drawing converted primitives. Cache clones share immutable auxiliary rows. No GPU layout, shader or layout promotion changes.\n\nNegative control: with a real continuous motion binding, the public non-compositor Path fixture leaked pixel (94,25) [250,0,5,255], expected [0,0,255,255], before wiring. Log: /private/tmp/blinc-motion-text-negative.log. An earlier synthetic CSS fixture failed its promotion assertion because the existing layout guard correctly refuses text subtrees; that was a fixture mismatch, not a rendering regression.\n\nThree GPU controls and one CPU guard control pass in storage and forced data-texture modes. The adjacent cached_text_clip_public_static_and_foreground_keep_rows GPU control passes in both modes. Commands selected blinc_app --lib with filters motion_text_clip and the one named cached-text control, --include-ignored/--ignored, --test-threads=1. CARGO_BUILD_JOBS=2, fallback primitive/glyph capacities 1024. No broad workspace, DSL, docs, platform or unrelated gates. Touched-file rustfmt and diff checks pass. Temporary renderer capability overrides restored.\n\nCoverage: public motion and surface-compositor entries with Path/Polygon, clips within motion wrappers and stationary outside ancestors, full and cache-eligible frames; directed translation values 0 -\u003e 18 -\u003e -6 -\u003e 0 at 1x/1.5x DPI; nonempty converted pool and no promoted-text patch records; transformed and ordinary retained snapshots; batch-local headers rebased after 2048 rows; filtering and replay after source invalidation and a poisoned 4096-row upload; pending damage scissors; shared-row identity retained over repeated dispatch. Pixel expectations use independent analytic triangle membership against an unclipped baseline, skip contour edges and require ink both inside and outside.\n\nThe existing css_layer_bakeable/css_active_patchable guards keep text subtrees off CSS promotion and in-place patching. The new CPU control preserves that contract. Existing active-binding repaint behavior stays in place. This slice does not add promoted-text clip ownership or live remapping, lift promotion guards, exercise spring ticks, redesign motion transforms, or claim universal effect/group isolation. If promoted text is enabled later, its legacy center/alpha patch needs coordinated clip-owner and full geometry remapping first. Browser/mobile pixels and performance remain unverified. Preparation, row uploads and reference counting remain unbenchmarked; replay shares immutable contour rows instead of cloning them.\n\nParent 732c3370857424d2e3c7ccfcde44fe0095471eda74dae4e5b415daca036738fe stays open for 3D text bakes with layer-local clip origins. Other clip shapes, general stacked intersections, decoration/shadow redesign, owner-gated shared ClipPath/CSS fill rules and cross-stream isolation on e0a7502 remain separate. Nothing pushed.","files":null}]}